Yes, this can be worked around with extension methods:

```csharp
public static class ResourceExtensions
{
    public static T Duplicate<T>(this Resource resource, bool deep = false) where T : class
    {
        return (T)resource.Duplicate(deep);
    }
}
```

However, this workaround has limitations:

**Fragmentation** - each project needs to implement its own extension

**Discovery** - not discoverable via IDE autocomplete like core API methods

**Consistency** - doesn't provide the unified API experience users expect from Godot

While the workaround is simple, having this as a core API feature provides a more polished and professional developer experience, especially for new users.
